From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0123] sweet: bind backboardd's render thread to an A76 by default (sweetfb_bind)

0118/0152 added sweetfb_bind: the backboardd thread that draws through eagl/Mesa
and calls SwapEnd is bound to cpu 7 (A76), and the panel copy's helpers and the
vsync tick to A55s. It was off by default and only tested with the boot arg.

0122b A/B (kernel 0122, 60 Hz, synthetic swipes, logs/xnu-0122r.txt and
xnu-0122b.txt): nonzero swaps/s avg 26.0 vs 21.7, p50 28 vs 23, p90 41 vs 33,
p95 43 vs 35, max 50 vs 44; the log confirms "backboardd's swapping thread ...
bound to cpu 7". The user judged the run visibly better.

0123 makes it the default; sweetfb_bind=0 keeps the old behaviour.
---
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -352,9 +352,12 @@
 	 * 0152: boot-arg sweetfb_bind=1: the thread of backboardd that swaps (CoreAnimation's render
 	 * server thread: it draws through eagl/Mesa and calls SwapEnd) is bound to the last processor,
 	 * a Cortex-A76 (sweetfb_render_cpu=N for another), and the panel copy's helpers and the vsync
-	 * tick to Cortex-A55s (cpu 2, 3, ... and 1), so they never take the A76 from it. Off by default.
+	 * tick to Cortex-A55s (cpu 2, 3, ... and 1), so they never take the A76 from it. On by
+	 * default (0123); sweetfb_bind=0 = old.
 	 */
 	fRenderCPU = 7;
+	/* 0123: on by default (0122b A/B: avg 26.0 vs 21.7 swaps/s, p90 41 vs 33); sweetfb_bind=0 = old */
+	fBind = 1;
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_bind", &fBind, sizeof(fBind));
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetfb_render_cpu", &fRenderCPU, sizeof(fRenderCPU));
 	if (fBind != 0 && fRenderCPU > ml_get_max_cpu_number()) {
